# =====================================================================
# FIXED x G8 / FIXED x XSEG-split combinations.  The fixed reservations
# join the SAME ledgers the dynamic passes consume (design §1.3 insertion
# order; §4.1 F13).  Two frozen consequences are asserted here:
#   * a fixed XDATA pin does NOT advance the dynamic XSEG cursor, but the
#     dynamic overlap check and the G8 retry ledger DO see the pin -- so a
#     pin is either overlap-free beside the dynamic range or a hard
#     failure (never a silent coexistence);
#   * s_XSEG/l_XSEG stay dynamic-only (F13), byte-identical to the
#     no-pin baseline.
# =====================================================================
# --- (1) FIXED-XDATA pin beside a dynamic XSEG slice in the same window:
# --- the slice takes the window base (the pin does not push it) and both
# --- ranges coexist overlap-free in the shared XDataUsed ledger.
